A growable sequence of bytes with a final zero byte.

Use alloc, core, and io.

A public record TcString has a data as a pointer to byte, a len as an unsigned number, and a cap as an unsigned number.

Publicly, to create an empty text, named str_new, returning TcString.
Let s be TcString.
Give back s.

Publicly, to create text from a pointer to byte p of length an unsigned number n, named str_from_bytes, returning TcString.
Call this as "create text from <p> of length <n>".
Let s be TcString.
Set s's len to n.
Set s's cap to n plus 1.
Let allocated be allocate s's cap bytes.
Set s's data to allocated.
If n is more than 0, copy n bytes from p to s's data.
Set item n of s's data to 0.
Give back s.

Publicly, to append to a string given s as a pointer to TcString, p as a pointer to byte, n as an unsigned number, named str_push_bytes, returning nothing.
Call this as "append <p> with length <n> to <s>".
If n equals 0, give back.
Let needed be s's len plus n plus 1.
If needed is more than s's cap.
Let new_cap be s's cap times 2.
If new_cap is less than needed, make new_cap needed.
If new_cap is less than 16, make new_cap 16 as an unsigned number.
Let old_cap be s's cap.
Let resized be resize memory at s's data from old_cap to new_cap.
Set s's data to resized.
Set s's cap to new_cap.
End the condition.
Copy n bytes from p to (s's data as an unsigned number plus s's len) as a pointer to byte.
Set s's len to s's len plus n.
Set item s's len of s's data to 0.

Publicly, to join a pointer to TcString a and a pointer to TcString b, named str_concat, returning TcString.
Call this as "join <a> and <b>".
Let joined be create text from a's data of length a's len.
append b's data with length b's len to address of joined.
Give back joined.

Publicly, to check whether a pointer to TcString a matches a pointer to TcString b, named str_eq, returning a truth value.
Call this as "text <a> matches text <b>".
If a's len is not equal to b's len, give back false.
Let i be 0 as an unsigned number.
While i is less than a's len.
If item i of a's data is not equal to item i of b's data, give back false.
Add 1 to i.
End the loop.
Give back true.

Publicly, to find the length of a pointer to TcString s, named str_len, returning an unsigned number.
Call this as "length of <s>".
Give back s's len.

Publicly, to copy a pointer to TcString s, named str_clone, returning TcString.
Call this as "copy text <s>".
Give back create text from s's data of length s's len.

Publicly, to clear a pointer to TcString s, named str_clear, returning nothing.
Call this as "clear text <s>".
Set s's len to 0 as an unsigned number.
If s's data is not empty, set item 0 of s's data to 0.

Publicly, to free a pointer to TcString s, named str_free, returning nothing.
Call this as "free text <s>".
If s's data is not empty, release memory at s's data.
Set s's data to no address.
Set s's len to 0 as an unsigned number.
Set s's cap to 0 as an unsigned number.

Publicly, to print a pointer to TcString s, named print_str, returning nothing.
You can call this as "say <s>", "show <s>", "print <s>", or "display <s>".
If s's len is more than 0, ask Linux kernel 1 with 1, s's data, and s's len.
Ask Linux kernel 1 with 1, "\n", and 1.
